description.en:
Places a detailed model on the left or right of a stand scene and sets its motion.
It waits for the model to load. With a base ID, it registers the speaker's name (CMND_ADD_TALK_CHARA(_hdl, "pname_" + _baseID)). It then picks a scale and a position from the character's body figure (CMND_GET_CHARA_FIGURE of _baseID, or of _ubaseID when _baseID is empty, figure 4 by default):
- figures 1, 4, 7: scale 0.9, position [-6.0, -11.0, -17.0], turned 30 degrees;
- figures 2, 3: scale 0.65, [-5.0, -10.0, -17.0];
- figures 5, 8: scale 0.8, [-6.0, -8.0, -17.0];
- figure 6: scale 0.98, [-5.5, -13.5, -17.0];
- the NPCs cn0013, cn0015, cn0019 and cn0045 have their own settings (scale 1.0).
On the right side (EV_CHARA_POS_RIGHT) the x position and the turn are mirrored. Finally it sets the motion with CMND_SET_MOTION_ID(_hdl, _motion[0], _motion[1], _motion[2], 0, 0).

examples.code:
WaitLoading(hTenmaH);
WaitLoading(hHarunaH);
SetHiMdlPosAndMotID(hTenmaH, EV_CHARA_POS_LEFT, [19, 1, 1], "cp0008");
SetHiMdlPosAndMotID(hHarunaH, EV_CHARA_POS_RIGHT, [41, 1, 1], "cn0004");
StartStandEvent();
